From 0fcb93b140426581138b0a2e7a60005a9027432e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 16:41:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/59] fix(polecat): protect live-session polecats from
 stall-recovery nuke (hq-zxhx)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stall-recovery reaped actively-running polecats that had no git commits yet
— an iris reviewer mid-review and two coders mid-implementation. Review
polecats (mol-polecat-review-pr) never commit, and a coder has a clean
worktree before its first commit, so loadFromBeads classified them StateIdle
and DecideWorkstate returned SAFE_TO_NUKE. The witness slot-open check then
nuked them, losing in-flight work.

A live, non-stale tmux session is the ground truth that the agent is working,
regardless of commit state. Thread that fact through:

- WorkstateInput.SessionRunning + Polecat.SessionRunning (also surfaced in
  `gt polecat list --json` as session_running).
- loadFromBeads derives sessionLive (tmux available + running + !stale) and
  sets it on every returned Polecat; workstateInputForPolecat and
  check-recovery populate the input from it.
- DecideWorkstate returns WORKING ("session-running") for an otherwise-idle
  polecat with a live session — never SAFE_TO_NUKE.

When tmux is nil (tests / no tmux) the flag stays false, so behavior is
unchanged. Adds a regression case to TestDecideWorkstateCanonicalFields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
